{
  "info": {
    "name": "HQ-ION: how select works (explainer)",
    "description": "A short walk-through for the dev lead: (1) the catalog list we publish, (2) the schema that defines the select JSON, (3) the select we send, (4) the on_select answer with eligible schemes, (5) a refused bad select.\n\nRun in order. Needs the ION testnet containers, the seller app (`npm start`) and the helper (`npm run listen`). Nothing here needs keys or a public address.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Is everything running?",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Seller app health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "Our seller app (NestJS, port 3102). If this fails: `npm run build && npm start` in HQ-ION.",
            "url": "{{seller_url}}/health"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('seller is up', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Test buyer / listener health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "The helper on port 3101 (`npm run listen`). It plays the BAP app and catches the on_select callback, which Postman cannot receive itself.",
            "url": "{{listener_url}}/catalog"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('listener is up', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. The catalog: the LIST of schemes we publish (shop window)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1a. Catalog contents: every scheme, same for everyone",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "STEP 1. This is what we publish with `npm run catalog:publish` and what ION's Discovery Service is meant to index. It lists ALL schemes with readable criteria only. It does NOT decide who qualifies: the thresholds stay inside our seller. A buyer sees this list after `discover`.",
            "url": "{{listener_url}}/catalog?lang=id"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('catalog lists schemes', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(b.schemes.length).to.be.above(0);",
                  "  console.log('catalog has', b.schemes.length, 'schemes');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "1b. The catalog index file (what a crawler fetches)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "The signed index file written by ION's seller adapter. A crawler reads this, then downloads the catalog files it points to (with digest and signature to verify).",
            "url": "{{proxy_url}}/beckn/index/becknCatalogs.index.json"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('index file served', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. The schema: what shape must the select JSON have?",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "2a. Profile schema (attributes.yaml)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "STEP 2. Every `...Attributes` block in a Beckn message has an `@context` URL. ION's adapter downloads the schema from that URL (only from allow-listed hosts) and validates our message against it. This is the schema for our `contractAttributes`: `msmeProfile` allows ONLY seven fields (businessType, sector, annualTurnoverIdr, province, workerCount, hasNIB, exportsOrPlansToExport) and `additionalProperties: false` refuses anything else. NOTE: this is OUR TEMPORARY stand-in, not an ION schema yet.",
            "url": "{{proxy_url}}/schema/HqMsmeProfile/v0/attributes.yaml"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('schema downloaded', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.include('msmeProfile');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2b. The JSON-LD context",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "The `@context` file that the select's `contractAttributes.@context` points to. It maps field names to meanings.",
            "url": "{{proxy_url}}/schema/HqMsmeProfile/v0/context.jsonld"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('context downloaded', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. The select: send the profile JSON",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "3a. select with an MSME profile (through the BUYER ADAPTER)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "description": "STEP 3. The real ION path: this call goes to the buyer adapter (:8081), which signs it, checks it against the schema from step 2, and forwards it through the seller adapter to our seller app. Look at `message.contract.contractAttributes.msmeProfile`: that is the profile. The response here is only an ACK. The answer is a separate on_select (next request).",
            "url": "{{bap_caller_url}}/select",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"context\": {\n    \"action\": \"select\",\n    \"version\": \"2.0.0\",\n    \"networkId\": \"{{network_id}}\",\n    \"bapId\": \"{{bap_id}}\",\n    \"bapUri\": \"{{bap_uri}}\",\n    \"bppId\": \"{{bpp_id}}\",\n    \"bppUri\": \"{{bpp_uri}}\",\n    \"transactionId\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n    \"messageId\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n    \"timestamp\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n    \"ttl\": \"PT30S\",\n    \"schemaContext\": []\n  },\n  \"message\": {\n    \"contract\": {\n      \"id\": \"check-1\",\n      \"participants\": [{ \"id\": \"buyer-1\", \"descriptor\": { \"code\": \"buyer\" } }],\n      \"commitments\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"commitment-1\",\n          \"status\": { \"code\": \"DRAFT\" },\n          \"resources\": [\n            {\n              \"id\": \"HQ-ELIGIBILITY-CHECK\",\n              \"descriptor\": { \"name\": \"Scheme eligibility check\" },\n              \"quantity\": { \"unitQuantity\": 1, \"unitCode\": \"UNIT\" }\n            }\n          ],\n          \"offer\": { \"id\": \"offer-eligibility\", \"resourceIds\": [\"HQ-ELIGIBILITY-CHECK\"] }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"contractAttributes\": {\n        \"@context\": \"{{schema_base_url}}/HqMsmeProfile/v0/context.jsonld\",\n        \"@type\": \"HqMsmeProfile\",\n        \"language\": \"id\",\n        \"msmeProfile\": {\n          \"businessType\": \"CV\",\n          \"sector\": \"craft\",\n          \"province\": \"Bali\",\n          \"workerCount\": 25,\n          \"annualTurnoverIdr\": 1500000000,\n          \"hasNIB\": true,\n          \"exportsOrPlansToExport\": true\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('HTTP 200 and ACK (this is only \"got it\", not the answer)', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().message.status).to.eql('ACK');",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) { pm.collectionVariables.set('last_message_id', pm.response.json().message.messageId); }"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "3b. The ANSWER (on_select) with the eligible schemes",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "STEP 4. Our seller ran the rules engine and sent `on_select` back through the adapters. The listener caught it; we fetch it by the messageId saved from 3a. See `contractAttributes.eligibility`: `eligibleCount`, `schemes[]` (each with `why`, `documents`, `fulfillment`) and `stillUnknownFields`. Keep `npm run listen` running.",
            "url": "{{listener_url}}/callbacks/{{last_message_id}}"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// the answer is sent just after the ACK; give it a moment to arrive",
                  "setTimeout(function () {}, 1500);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('on_select arrived with eligible schemes', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.context.action).to.eql('on_select');",
                  "  const e = body.message.contract.contractAttributes.eligibility;",
                  "  pm.expect(e.eligibleCount).to.be.above(0);",
                  "  console.log('eligible:', e.schemes.map(s => s.id).join(', '));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Why the schema matters: a bad select is refused",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "4a. select with a phone number (refused by the schema)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "description": "Same select plus `phoneNumber`. The schema from step 2 has `additionalProperties: false`, so the buyer adapter refuses it with SCH_FIELD_NOT_ALLOWED and it never reaches our seller. This is how personal data is kept out by design.",
            "url": "{{bap_caller_url}}/select",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"context\": {\n    \"action\": \"select\",\n    \"version\": \"2.0.0\",\n    \"networkId\": \"{{network_id}}\",\n    \"bapId\": \"{{bap_id}}\",\n    \"bapUri\": \"{{bap_uri}}\",\n    \"bppId\": \"{{bpp_id}}\",\n    \"bppUri\": \"{{bpp_uri}}\",\n    \"transactionId\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n    \"messageId\": \"{{$guid}}\",\n    \"timestamp\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n    \"ttl\": \"PT30S\",\n    \"schemaContext\": []\n  },\n  \"message\": {\n    \"contract\": {\n      \"id\": \"check-1\",\n      \"participants\": [{ \"id\": \"buyer-1\", \"descriptor\": { \"code\": \"buyer\" } }],\n      \"commitments\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"commitment-1\",\n          \"status\": { \"code\": \"DRAFT\" },\n          \"resources\": [\n            {\n              \"id\": \"HQ-ELIGIBILITY-CHECK\",\n              \"descriptor\": { \"name\": \"Scheme eligibility check\" },\n              \"quantity\": { \"unitQuantity\": 1, \"unitCode\": \"UNIT\" }\n            }\n          ],\n          \"offer\": { \"id\": \"offer-eligibility\", \"resourceIds\": [\"HQ-ELIGIBILITY-CHECK\"] }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"contractAttributes\": {\n        \"@context\": \"{{schema_base_url}}/HqMsmeProfile/v0/context.jsonld\",\n        \"@type\": \"HqMsmeProfile\",\n        \"language\": \"id\",\n        \"msmeProfile\": {\n          \"businessType\": \"CV\",\n          \"sector\": \"craft\",\n          \"province\": \"Bali\",\n          \"workerCount\": 25,\n          \"annualTurnoverIdr\": 1500000000,\n          \"hasNIB\": true,\n          \"exportsOrPlansToExport\": true,\n          \"phoneNumber\": \"+628123456789\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('refused (not 200)', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.within(400, 499);",
                  "  console.log(pm.response.text().slice(0, 300));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "seller_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:3102"
    },
    {
      "key": "listener_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:3101"
    },
    {
      "key": "bap_caller_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8081/bap/caller"
    },
    {
      "key": "proxy_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:9000"
    },
    {
      "key": "network_id",
      "value": "ion.id/staging"
    },
    {
      "key": "bap_id",
      "value": "dc-bap.ion.id"
    },
    {
      "key": "bap_uri",
      "value": "http://reverse-proxy:9000/bap/receiver"
    },
    {
      "key": "bpp_id",
      "value": "dc-bpp.ion.id"
    },
    {
      "key": "bpp_uri",
      "value": "http://reverse-proxy:9000/bpp/receiver"
    },
    {
      "key": "schema_base_url",
      "value": "http://reverse-proxy:9000/schema"
    },
    {
      "key": "last_message_id",
      "value": ""
    }
  ]
}